#: ../../../faq/troubleshooting.rst:13
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/troubleshooting.rst:16
msgid "Package Manager"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/troubleshooting.rst:21
msgid "[Error 5] Access is denied"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/troubleshooting.rst:23
msgid ""
"PlatformIO installs all packages to \":ref:`projectconf_pio_core_dir`/"
"packages\" directory. You **MUST HAVE** write access to this folder. Please "
"note that **PlatformIO does not require** \"sudo\"/administrative privileges."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/troubleshooting.rst:31
msgid "Solution 1: Remove folder"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/troubleshooting.rst:33
msgid ""
"A quick solution is to remove \":ref:`projectconf_pio_core_dir`/packages\" "
"folder and repeat installation/building/uploading again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/troubleshooting.rst:37
msgid "Solution 2: Antivirus"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/troubleshooting.rst:39
msgid ""
"Some antivirus tools forbid programs to create files in the background. "
"PlatformIO Package Manager does all work in the background: downloads "
"package, unpacks archive in temporary folder and moves final files to \":ref:"
"`projectconf_pio_core_dir`/packages\" folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/troubleshooting.rst:44
msgid ""
"Antivirus tool can block PlatformIO, that is why you see \"[Error 5] Access "
"is denied\". Try to **disable it for a while** or add :ref:"
"`projectconf_pio_core_dir` directory to exclusion/whitelist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/troubleshooting.rst:49
msgid "Solution 3: Run from Terminal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/troubleshooting.rst:51
msgid ""
"As we mentioned in \"Solution 2\", antivirus tools can block background file "
"system operations. Another solution is to run :ref:`piocore` from a system "
"terminal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/troubleshooting.rst:54
msgid ""
"Open **System Terminal**, on Windows ``cmd.exe`` (not :ref:`pioide` Terminal)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/troubleshooting.rst:55
msgid ""
"Build a project and upload firmware using :ref:`piocore` which will download "
"and install all dependent packages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/troubleshooting.rst:69
msgid ""
"If \"pio\" command is not globally available in your environment and you "
"use :ref:`pioide`, please use built-in :ref:`piocore` which is located in:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/troubleshooting.rst:72
msgid ""
"Windows: ``C:\\Users\\{username}\\.platformio\\penv\\Scripts\\platformio`` "
"Please replace ``{username}`` with a real user name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/troubleshooting.rst:74
msgid "Unix: ``~/.platformio/penv/bin/platformio``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/troubleshooting.rst:78
msgid ""
"You can add ``platformio`` and ``pio`` commands to your system environment. "
"See :ref:`piocore_install_shell_commands`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/troubleshooting.rst:82
msgid "Building"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/troubleshooting.rst:85
msgid "UnicodeWarning: Unicode equal comparison failed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/troubleshooting.rst:87
msgid ""
"Full warning message is \"UnicodeWarning: Unicode equal comparison failed to "
"convert both arguments to Unicode - interpreting them as being unequal\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/troubleshooting.rst:90
msgid ""
"**KNOWN ISSUE**. Please move your project to a folder which full path does "
"not contain non-ASCII chars."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/troubleshooting.rst:94
msgid "UnicodeDecodeError: Non-ASCII characters found in build environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/troubleshooting.rst:96
msgid ""
"**KNOWN ISSUE**. :ref:`piocore` currently does not support projects which "
"contain non-ASCII characters (codes) in a full path or depend on the "
"libraries which use non-ASCII characters in their names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/troubleshooting.rst:100
msgid "**TEMPORARY SOLUTION**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/troubleshooting.rst:102
msgid ""
"Use :ref:`pioide`, it will automatically install :ref:`piocore` in a root of "
"system disk (``%DISK%/.platformio``) and avoid an issue when system User "
"contains non-ASCII characters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/troubleshooting.rst:105
msgid ""
"Do not use non-ASCII characters in project folder name or its parent folders."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/troubleshooting.rst:107
msgid "Also, if you want to place :ref:`piocore` in own location, see:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/troubleshooting.rst:109
msgid "Set :envvar:`PLATFORMIO_CORE_DIR` environment variable with own path"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/troubleshooting.rst:110
msgid ""
"Configure custom location per project using :ref:`projectconf_pio_core_dir` "
"option in :ref:`projectconf`."
msgstr ""

